WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:14.005
main launches runKernel with one warp of 32 threads. stride sets the distance between input indices, while output remains contiguous. n counts outputs; the input allocation must also cover the largest strided read.

00:00:14.005 --> 00:00:17.245
The host groups returned indices into sectors.

00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:20.235
Lane addresses.

00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:23.260
Each lane selects input[lane × stride].

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.785
Group addresses.

00:00:24.785 --> 00:00:27.455
Aligned sectors group the requested words.

00:00:27.455 --> 00:00:28.810
Return values.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.825
Each lane writes its contiguous output slot.

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.900
One warp issues a load with an address for each active lane.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.170
The memory path groups these addresses into requests.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:46.560
Caches may supply data before device memory is accessed; a sector count does not measure device-memory traffic.
